  "guide.productiveslimes.page.1": "§2§lProductive Slimes§r\n\nRaise slimes that make resources.\n\nThis guide covers the basics. With JEI installed, press R on a spawn egg or slime jar to see how to breed it.",
  "guide.productiveslimes.page.10": "§2§lSlime Squeezer§r\n\nPress slimeballs into their resource: an Iron Slimeball gives an Iron Ingot, a Stone Slimeball gives 2 Stone.",
  "guide.productiveslimes.page.11": "§2§lSpeed Upgrades§r\n\nThe Slime Pen and the Slime Squeezer each take two upgrades. Speed: 25% faster. Advanced: twice as fast. Two upgrades stack.",
  "guide.productiveslimes.page.12": "§2§lAutomation§r\n\nHoppers and pipes work.\n\nPen: jars go in the top, food in the sides, slimeballs come out the bottom.\n\nSqueezer: slimeballs go in the top or sides, results come out the bottom.",
  "guide.productiveslimes.page.2": "§2§lThe Slimy Land§r\n\nA bright green biome found in mild climates. Wild productive slimes only spawn here, and Slime Crystal Ore only forms here, inside Slimy Stone.",
  "guide.productiveslimes.page.3": "§2§lSlime Crystal§r\n\nMine Slime Crystal Ore with a stone pickaxe or better. Crystal goes into jars, pens, squeezers and upgrades. Slime Shrines hold a few too.",
  "guide.productiveslimes.page.4": "§2§lSlime Jar§r\n\nRight-click a productive slime with an empty jar to catch it. Right-click a block to let it out. The jar keeps the slime's type, size and name.",
  "guide.productiveslimes.page.5": "§2§lFeeding§r\n\nEach slime eats one food: a Stone Slime eats cobblestone. A size 1 slime grows to size 2 after 4 food. Sneak-feed an adult to grow it: 8 food to size 3, 12 to size 4.",
  "guide.productiveslimes.page.6": "§2§lBreeding§r\n\nFeed two adults (size 2+) their food. They find each other and make a size 1 baby, then rest for 5 minutes.",
  "guide.productiveslimes.page.7": "§2§lCatalysts§r\n\nMost recipes need a block within 2 blocks of the parents. Stone + Stone next to Andesite makes an Andesite Slime. Two of one type make that type when no catalyst matches.",
  "guide.productiveslimes.page.8": "§2§lSlime Pen§r\n\nPut a filled jar in a pen. Every batch gives one slimeball per slime size, so grow your slimes before penning them.",
  "guide.productiveslimes.page.9": "§2§lPen Food§r\n\nPut the slime's food in the pen's food slot. One item keeps the slime fed for 4 batches, and fed batches run twice as fast.",
